# Component Testing Rules

## Testing Philosophy

### Focus on Business Logic

Write tests that verify **business logic** and **user-facing behavior**. Tests should validate that the component works correctly from the user's perspective.

```typescript
// ✅ Good - tests business logic
it('displays error message when API call fails', async () => {
  (ApiModule.fetchData as Mock).mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('Failed'))
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  await nextTick()
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="error-message"]').exists()).toBe(true)
})

// ✅ Good - tests user interaction
it('submits form when submit button is clicked', async () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  await wrapper.find('[data-test="submit-button"]').trigger('click')
  expect(wrapper.emitted('submit')).toBeTruthy()
})

// ❌ Bad - testing library implementation
it('calls nextTick', async () => {
  await nextTick()
  // This doesn't test anything meaningful
})

// ❌ Bad - testing that Vue works
it('renders component', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  expect(wrapper.exists()).toBe(true)
  // This just tests that Vue can render, not our code
})
```

### Avoid Empty Tests

Don't write tests just to increase coverage. Every test should verify meaningful behavior:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - empty test that doesn't verify anything
it('renders component', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  // No assertions, just checking it doesn't crash
})

// ✅ Good - test verifies specific behavior
it('renders form fields in create mode', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="title-input"]').exists()).toBe(true)
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="description-input"]').exists()).toBe(true)
})
```

### Don't Test Third-Party Libraries

Don't test that libraries work - they have their own tests. Test how your component uses them:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - testing that Element Plus works
it('ElInput receives modelValue prop', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  const input = wrapper.findComponent({ name: 'ElInput' })
  expect(input.props('modelValue')).toBe('test')
  // This just tests Element Plus, not our logic
})

// ✅ Good - testing our component's behavior with ElInput
it('updates modelValue when user types in input', async () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  const input = wrapper.find('[data-test="title-input"]')
  await input.setValue('New Title')
  expect(wrapper.emitted('update:modelValue')).toBeTruthy()
})
```

### Don't Chase Coverage Metrics

Code coverage is a tool, not a goal. Focus on testing critical paths and edge cases:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad - writing tests for every getter/setter
it('has getter for title', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  expect(wrapper.vm.title).toBeDefined()
})

// ✅ Good - testing that title affects rendering
it('displays title in header when provided', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory({ title: 'Test Title' })
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="header"]').text()).toContain('Test Title')
})
```

### Test User Scenarios

Write tests that reflect real user workflows:

```typescript
// ✅ Good - tests complete user flow
it('allows user to create campaign with required fields', async () => {
  const { wrapper, store } = factory()
  
  // User fills form
  await wrapper.find('[data-test="title-input"]').setValue('Campaign Title')
  await wrapper.find('[data-test="description-input"]').setValue('Description')
  
  // User submits
  await wrapper.find('[data-test="submit-button"]').trigger('click')
  
  // Verify result
  expect(store.createCampaign).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
    title: 'Campaign Title',
    description: 'Description',
  })
})
```

## Test File Structure

### Basic Imports

```typescript
import { nextTick } from 'vue'
import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils'
import { beforeEach, describe, expect, it, vi, type Mock } from 'vitest'
import { createTestingPinia } from '@pinia/testing'
```

### Using describe

Group component tests in a `describe` block. The describe block name should include the **section name** and **component name**:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - includes section and component name
describe('FormAdset Performance Component', () => {
  // tests
})

describe('Streamer Campaigns CurrentPlatform Component', () => {
  // tests
})

describe('FormDescription Component', () => {
  // tests
})

// ✅ Correct - for deeply nested components, include full path
describe('Streamer Campaigns AdsetInfo Info BrandAwareness PPVA', () => {
  // tests
})

describe('Streamer Link Alerts Supporters', () => {
  // tests
})

// ❌ Incorrect - missing section context
describe('Performance', () => {
  // tests
})

// ❌ Incorrect - too generic
describe('Component', () => {
  // tests
})
```

**Naming Pattern:**
- Format: `'SectionName ComponentName Component'` or `'Module Section ComponentName'`
- Include enough context to identify where the component is located
- For nested components, include the full path: `'Module Section Subsection ComponentName'`
- Always end with the component name (optionally add "Component" suffix for clarity)

### Factory Pattern

Use a factory function to create wrappers with configurable parameters:

```typescript
const factory = (props = {}, storeState = {}) => {
  const wrapper = mount(Component, {
    global: {
      plugins: [
        i18n,
        createTestingPinia({
          createSpy: vi.fn,
          initialState: {
            'store-name': storeState,
          },
        }),
      ],
      stubs: {
        // component mocks
      },
    },
    props: { ...props },
  })

  const store = useStore()

  return { wrapper, store }
}
```

### beforeEach

Always clear mocks before each test:

```typescript
beforeEach(() => {
  vi.clearAllMocks()
})
```

## Component Mounting

### Using mount

Use `mount` from `@vue/test-utils` to mount components:

```typescript
const wrapper = mount(Component, {
  global: {
    plugins: [i18n, createTestingPinia({ createSpy: vi.fn })],
  },
  props: {
    propName: 'value',
  },
})
```

### Configuring Plugins

Connect necessary plugins:

- `i18n` - for internationalization
- `createTestingPinia` - for testing Pinia stores

```typescript
global: {
  plugins: [
    i18n,
    createTestingPinia({
      createSpy: vi.fn,
      initialState: {
        'store-name': {
          // initial store state
        },
      },
    }),
  ],
}
```

### Stubs for Child Components

Create stubs for child components to isolate the component under test:

```typescript
stubs: {
  ChildComponent: {
    name: 'ChildComponent',
    template: '<div data-test="child-component"></div>',
    props: ['prop1', 'prop2'],
    emits: ['update:modelValue'],
  },
}
```

## Element Selectors

### Using data-test Attributes

Always use `data-test` attributes instead of classes or other selectors:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="component-name"]').exists()).toBe(true)

// ❌ Incorrect
expect(wrapper.find('.component-class').exists()).toBe(true)
expect(wrapper.find('#component-id').exists()).toBe(true)
```

### Finding Elements and Components

```typescript
// Find element by data-test
const element = wrapper.find('[data-test="element-name"]')

// Find component
const component = wrapper.findComponent({ name: 'ComponentName' })
const componentByDataTest = wrapper.findComponent('[data-test="component-name"]')

// Check existence
expect(element.exists()).toBe(true)
expect(component.exists()).toBe(false)
```

## Mocks

### Mocking Modules

Use `vi.mock()` to mock modules at the beginning of the file:

```typescript
vi.mock('@/core/helpers')
vi.mock('@/modules/.../api')
vi.mock('vue-router', async () => {
  const actual = await vi.importActual<typeof import('vue-router')>('vue-router')
  return {
    ...actual,
    useRoute: vi.fn(),
    useRouter: vi.fn(),
  }
})
```

### Component Mocks

Create mock components with `data-test` attributes:

```typescript
const mockComponent = {
  name: 'ComponentName',
  template: '<div data-test="component-name"><slot /></div>',
  props: ['modelValue', 'disabled'],
  emits: ['update:modelValue'],
}
```

For multiple components, use a loop:

```typescript
const formComponents = ['FormTitle', 'FormDescription', 'FormPlatform']

const formComponentMocks: Record<string, any> = {}
formComponents.forEach(component => {
  formComponentMocks[component] = {
    name: component,
    template: `<div data-test="${component}"></div>`,
    props: ['modelValue'],
    emits: ['update:modelValue'],
  }
})
```

### Mocking Stores

Use `createTestingPinia` to mock stores:

```typescript
createTestingPinia({
  createSpy: vi.fn,
  initialState: {
    'store-name': {
      data: null,
      loading: false,
    },
  },
})
```

After mounting, you can access the store and change its state:

```typescript
const store = useStore()
store.data = mockData
await nextTick()
```

### API Endpoint Mocks

Mock API modules to isolate the component from real API calls:

```typescript
import * as ApiModule from '@/modules/.../api'
import type { Mock } from 'vitest'

vi.mock('@/modules/.../api')
```

In tests, use `mockResolvedValueOnce` for successful responses and `mockRejectedValueOnce` for errors:

```typescript
// Successful response
(ApiModule.getData as Mock).mockResolvedValueOnce(mockData)

// Error
const error = new Error('API Error')
(ApiModule.getData as Mock).mockRejectedValueOnce(error)
```

Verify API method calls:

```typescript
expect(ApiModule.getData).toHaveBeenCalledWith(param1, param2)
expect(ApiModule.getData).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1)
```

### Data Mocks

Create constants with test data at the beginning of the test file:

```typescript
// Simple data mocks
const mockSegment = {
  id: 1,
  title: 'Gaming Segment',
  streamers: [
    { id: 1, name: 'Streamer 1' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Streamer 2' },
  ],
} as ISegment

const mockCreative = {
  title: 'Test Creative Title',
  slug: 'creative-123',
}
```

Use fixtures from `fixtures/` folders in API modules:

```typescript
import { performanceCampaign } from '@/modules/Partner/views/FormCampaign/api/getPerformanceCampaign/fixtures/performanceCampaign'
import { performanceAdset } from '@/modules/Partner/views/FormAdset/api/getPerformanceAdset/fixtures/performanceAdset'

// Usage in tests
formCampaignStore.campaign = performanceCampaign
formAdsetStore.adset = performanceAdset
```

Data mocks should contain only the minimum necessary fields for the test. Don't create excessive data.

## Behavior Testing

### Testing Props

Verify prop passing and usage:

```typescript
it('receives and uses props correctly', () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory({
    modelValue: { title: 'Test' },
  })

  expect(wrapper.props('modelValue').title).toBe('Test')
})
```

### Testing Events (Emits)

Verify event emission:

```typescript
it('emits update:modelValue when value changes', async () => {
  const { wrapper } = factory()
  const input = wrapper.find('[data-test="input"]')

  await input.setValue('new value')

  expect(wrapper.emitted('update:modelValue')).toBeTruthy()
  expect(wrapper.emitted('update:modelValue')[0]).toEqual(['new value'])
})
```

### Testing Conditional Rendering

Use `nextTick()` to wait for DOM updates after changing reactive data:

```typescript
it('renders component when condition is met', async () => {
  const { wrapper, store } = factory()

  store.currentCampaignType = CampaignType.BRAND_AWARENESS
  await nextTick()

  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="brand-awareness-form"]').exists()).toBe(true)
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="performance-form"]').exists()).toBe(false)
})
```

### Testing Store Interactions

Verify store changes and component reactions:

```typescript
it('updates when store changes', async () => {
  const { wrapper, store } = factory()

  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="component"]').exists()).toBe(false)

  store.data = mockData
  await nextTick()

  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="component"]').exists()).toBe(true)
})
```

## Examples

### Complete Factory Function Example

```typescript
describe('FormComponent', () => {
  const factory = (routeName = RouteName.CREATE, storeState = {}) => {
    vi.mocked(useRoute).mockReturnValue({
      name: routeName,
      params: {},
      query: {},
    } as any)

    const wrapper = mount(FormComponent, {
      global: {
        plugins: [
          i18n,
          createTestingPinia({
            createSpy: vi.fn,
            initialState: {
              'form-store': {
                currentType: null,
                ...storeState,
              },
            },
          }),
        ],
        stubs: {
          ElForm: {
            name: 'ElForm',
            template: '<form><slot /></form>',
          },
          FormField: {
            name: 'FormField',
            template: '<div data-test="form-field"></div>',
            props: ['modelValue'],
          },
        },
      },
    })

    const formStore = useFormStore()

    if (routeName === RouteName.EDIT) {
      formStore.data = mockData
    }

    return { wrapper, formStore }
  }

  beforeEach(() => {
    vi.clearAllMocks()
  })

  it('renders form in create mode', () => {
    const { wrapper } = factory()
    expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="form"]').exists()).toBe(true)
  })
})
```

### API Mocks Test Example

```typescript
import * as SegmentsApi from '@/modules/Partner/views/Segments/api'
import type { Mock } from 'vitest'

vi.mock('@/modules/Partner/views/Segments/api')

describe('Component with API', () => {
  const mockSegment = {
    id: 1,
    title: 'Test Segment',
  } as ISegment

  it('fetches and displays data', async () => {
    (SegmentsApi.getSegment as Mock).mockResolvedValueOnce(mockSegment)

    const { wrapper } = factory()
    await nextTick()

    expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="segment-title"]').text()).toBe('Test Segment')
    expect(SegmentsApi.getSegment).toHaveBeenCalledWith(1)
  })

  it('handles API error', async () => {
    const error = new Error('API Error')
    (SegmentsApi.getSegment as Mock).mockRejectedValueOnce(error)

    const { wrapper } = factory()
    await nextTick()

    expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="error"]').exists()).toBe(true)
  })
})
```

### Conditional Rendering Test Example

```typescript
it('renders different components based on store state', async () => {
  const { wrapper, store } = factory()

  // Initially nothing is rendered
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="form"]').exists()).toBe(false)

  // BrandAwareness is rendered
  store.currentCampaignType = CampaignType.BRAND_AWARENESS
  await nextTick()
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="brand-awareness-form"]').exists()).toBe(true)
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="performance-form"]').exists()).toBe(false)

  // Changes to Performance
  store.currentCampaignType = CampaignType.PERFORMANCE
  await nextTick()
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="brand-awareness-form"]').exists()).toBe(false)
  expect(wrapper.find('[data-test="performance-form"]').exists()).toBe(true)
})
```
